s($,"c7f","bQn",()=>{var q="Bavarian Illuminati",p="Gnomes of Zurich",o="Rosicrucians",n="Keep your notes secure, warning him against occult prying.",m="Carbonari"
return A.a([A.kk("Reassure him that it is simple, harmless phosphorescent science.","Warn him that the secrets of the Manor are not for the eyes of prying priests.","cottage_gregor","Glarus","My child, the local parishioners are terrified of unholy, glowing lights emanating from the Manor's basement. I must ask what profane experiments you are conducting in this holy valley.","Father Gregor Zweifel",new A.aLr(),new A.aLs(),"The priest seems mollified by your calm, scientific explanation. (+0.2 Glarus Standing)","The priest shivers and backs away, eyes narrowed in suspicion. (-0.2 Glarus Standing)"),A.kk("Sign the pledge and promise obedience to the Superiors.","Assert your intellectual independence and refuse to act under another's direction.","cottage_fritz",q,"Greetings. I am Fritz, an initiate under the direction of the Superiors of the Order. We are organizing a secret network of local eyes to perfect human nature and achieve harmony with nature. I demand you pledge to read and think precisely what the Superiors prescribe.","Professor Fritz Weishaupt",new A.aLt(),new A.aLE(),"Fritz nods, satisfied. He hands you a list of mandatory readings. (+0.2 Bavarian Illuminati Standing)","Fritz glares, warning that those who reject the sun of reason shall remain in the dark. (-0.2 Bavarian Illuminati Standing)"),A.kk("Pledge that Glarus will always honor noble blood.","Tell her that the age of kings has passed.","cottage_antoinette","Chevaliers de la foi","Ah, the master of the Manor. I am Countess Antoinette, exiled from my beloved France by the vulgar revolutionary mob. I seek elegant allies to fund a royalist counter-revolution and restore the crown. Will you support our noble cause?","Countess Antoinette de Bertier",new A.aLO(),new A.aLP(),"She curtsies elegantly, pleased by your refined demeanor. (+0.2 Chevaliers de la foi Standing)","She gasps, calling you a peasant sympathizer, and sweeps away. (-0.2 Chevaliers de la foi Standing)"),A.kk("Sign the banking partnership to secure your financial future.","Reject their credit, declaring that Glarus answers to no banker.","cottage_regina",p,"Business at last. I am Regina, coordinating secret vaults for the Gnomes. Your Manor holds considerable land value, but also significant liabilities. We are offering a lines-of-credit partnership. Shall we agree to secure your assets?","Baroness Regina von Stauffacher",new A.aLQ(),new A.aLR(),"She smiles coldly, registering your signature in her ledger. (+0.2 Gnomes of Zurich Standing)","She closes her ledger, warning that unpaid debts have a habit of accumulating. (-0.2 Gnomes of Zurich Standing)"),A.kk("Open your scientific archives to the mystic alchemist.",n,"cottage_johannes",o,"Peace be upon this house. I am Johannes, a simple hermit seeking the alchemical transformation of the soul. I have sensed deep spiritual resonances within your laboratory. Will you permit me to study your research notes in pursuit of the Great Work?","Johannes the Hermit",new A.aLS(),new A.aLT(),"He bows deeply, offering a silent blessing for your generosity. (+0.2 Rosicrucians Standing)","He sighs, noting that the path to true wisdom is often locked by fear. (-0.2 Rosicrucians Standing)"),A.kk("Promise to provide weapons and harbor their fighters.","Warn them that Glarus will not harbor violent rebels.","cottage_seamus","Fenian Brotherhood","Aye, you must be the landlord. I am Seamus, representing the Fenian Brotherhood. We are preparing a grand uprising against the oppressors, and we need iron and powder. Help us arm the rebellion, and we will remember our friends.","Seamus O'Connor",new A.aLU(),new A.aLu(),'He clasps your hand with a fierce grin. "For freedom, then!" (+0.2 Fenian Brotherhood Standing)',"He spits on the floor, warning that those who stand with the crown will burn with it. (-0.2 Fenian Brotherhood Standing)"),A.kk("Promise to limit logging and protect the sacred groves.","Declare that the estate's resources belong to the Manor.","cottage_elspeth","Ancient Order of Foresters","Halt, city dweller. I am Elspeth of the Foresters. Your servants have been felling trees and disturbing the ancient spirits of the wood. The grove demands you cease your logging and respect the ancient boundaries of the valley.","Elspeth Luchsinger",new A.aLv(),new A.aLw(),"She relaxes, her eyes softening as she whistles to her bear companion. (+0.2 Foresters Standing)","She glares, warning that the forest remembers every axe blow. (-0.2 Foresters Standing)"),A.kk("Pledge to improve servant wages and support labor unions.","Warn him that the Manor operates under strict hierarchy.","cottage_giuseppe",m,"Salute, comrade. I am Giuseppe. We are the Carbonari, the charcoal burners who spark the flames of liberty! We are organizing the workers of the valley to rise against their masters. Will you stand with the working class, or are you a tyrant?","Giuseppe Rossi",new A.aLx(),new A.aLy(),"He raises a fist, shouting a cheer for the revolution! (+0.2 Carbonari Standing)","He scowls, declaring that the aristocracy will be the first to meet the flames. (-0.2 Carbonari Standing)"),A.kk("Open your laboratory doors to the Templar knights.","Assert that the laboratory is private scientific ground.","cottage_godfrey","Knights Templar","In the name of the Temple, greetings. I am Godfrey, hunting the occult anomalies that plague this valley. Your scientific endeavors border on the heretical. Will you submit your laboratory for a Templar inspection to ensure purity?","Godfrey de Molay",new A.aLz(),new A.aLA(),"He nods grimly, his knights marching in to inspect the rooms. (+0.2 Knights Templar Standing)","He lays a hand on his sword hilt, warning that heresy will be purged. (-0.2 Knights Templar Standing)"),A.kk("Express interest in the occult and agree to participate in rituals.","Assert that Glarus relies on empirical science, not magic.","cottage_lilith","Golden Dawn","Greetings, traveler. I am Lilith of the Golden Dawn. I have traversed the astral planes to find you. Your soul holds a rare resonance, capable of anchoring great magic. Will you join our hermetic circle and explore the mysteries of the unseen?","Lilith Crowley",new A.aLB(),new A.aLC(),"She smiles mysteriously, her eyes flashing with otherworldly light. (+0.2 Golden Dawn Standing)","She sighs, warning that those who rely only on sight are blind to the universe. (-0.2 Golden Dawn Standing)"),A.kk("Assure her that your studies are a noble pursuit to understand nature and ease human suffering.","Proclaim that you will find a way to conquer mortality and bring back what was lost, at any cost.","cottage_mary","Glarus","My child, I have heard of the tragedy that befell your family. In times of such deep sorrow, the mind can wander to very dark places. Please tell me you are not letting your grief lead you down a path of obsession.","Mary Shelley",new A.aLD(),new A.aLF(),'Mary sighs softly, touching your arm with her pale hand. "Grief makes monsters of us all. Be careful, creator." (+0.20 Glarus Standing)','Mary draws back, her eyes filled with concern and fear. "To defy the natural order is to invite your own destruction." (-0.20 Glarus Standing)'),A.kk("Enthusiastically agree and pledge your laboratory resources to his electrical research.","Dismiss his theories as romantic poetry; assert your focus is purely empirical chemistry.","cottage_percy",q,"Ah, creator! Your research into vitalism is magnificent. Galvani's frog muscles and Erasmus Darwin's spontaneous generation prove that electricity is the vital fluid analogous to the human soul. Let us collaborate and build a Leyden Jar grid to capture the lightning!","Percy Bysshe Shelley",new A.aLG(),new A.aLH(),"Percy beams with excitement, gesturing to his sketches of atmospheric conductor grids. (+0.20 Bavarian Illuminati Standing)","Percy scowls, calling your science unimaginative and pedantic before pocketing his journals. (-0.20 Bavarian Illuminati Standing)"),A.kk("Accept his funding, welcoming his aristocratic patronage to double your resources.","Refuse his money, stating that Frankenstein Manor is not a toy for bored lords.","cottage_byron",p,"Business at last. I have run from suffocating debt and societal rumors in London to Diodati. Your estate is fine, but lacks capital. I offer massive venture funding for your unholy marvels, but expect full partnership. Do we strike a deal?","Lord Byron",new A.aLI(),new A.aLJ(),"Byron laughs heartily, signing a draft for gold reserves in his ledger. (+0.20 Gnomes of Zurich Standing)","Byron sneers, muttering that your pride matches your poverty, and snaps his ledger shut. (-0.20 Gnomes of Zurich Standing)"),A.kk("Agree to assist the Carbonari network and provide cover for her operations.","Decline to get involved in local insurgencies and marital disputes.","cottage_claire",m,"Greetings. I am Claire. My daughter Allegra is held by Byron's cruel command in a remote convent, and local peasants are crushed by local taxes. I coordinate the Carbonari charcoal-burners lodge in the Jura woods. Help me harbor resources, and we will guide your paths through the wild.","Claire Clairmont",new A.aLK(),new A.aLL(),"Claire raises a clenched hand in solidarity, sharing a map of secret forest passes. (+0.20 Carbonari Standing)","Claire glares at you, warning that those who ignore the Carbonari will find no safety in the woods. (-0.20 Carbonari Standing)"),A.kk("Open your anatomical research files to the cynical physician.",n,"cottage_polidori",o,"Greetings, colleague. I am Polidori, Byron's physician. I study the siphoning of organic tissue\u2014the modern vampire. My medical notebooks contain alchemical and biological repair formulas that can heal your creations. Will you share your research files with me?","Dr. John Polidori",new A.aLM(),new A.aLN(),"Polidori nods grimly, sharing a treatise on blood-siphoning algorithms. (+0.20 Rosicrucians Standing)","Polidori sneers, noting that a plagiarist's shadow makes everyone paranoid. (-0.20 Rosicrucians Standing)")],A.aE("K<Bu>"))})
s($,"c59","bGW",()=>A.Jl(null))
s($,"c5a","bGX",()=>A.a([A.ado("THE PRINCIPLES OF CIVIC JURISPRUDENCE\n\n1. THE NATURE OF CONTRACTS: A covenant is legally established only when there is a clear, uncoerced Offer, a mutual and uncoerced Acceptance, and a valuable Consideration (representing a dynamic exchange of value, whether alchemical reagents, land, or coin). Without all three elements, no covenant stands.\n\n2. HEARSAY AND ADMISSIBILITY: Hearsay refers to any out-of-court statement offered by a witness in a trial to establish the absolute truth of the matter asserted. Such statements are fundamentally inadmissible due to the lack of direct cross-examination, unless they fall under a specific, recognized exception (such as dying declarations or business ledgers).\n\n3. DEGREE OF KINSHIP: Kinship consanguinity is calculated by tracing up to a common ancestor and down to the relation. Your grandmother's cousin's granddaughter is classified precisely in the sixth degree of consanguinity, commonly referred to in modern law as a second cousin once removed.\n\n4. ADVERSE POSSESSION: Land acquisition by continuous occupation requires uninterrupted, open, and hostile possession for a period of twenty consecutive years. If the landowner does not object within this twenty-year term, title passes to the occupier.","TOME I: JURISPRUDENCE & THE COVENANT OF THE CONTRACT"),A.ado("ALCHEMICAL KINETICS & PHARMACY\n\n1. THE PH LOGARITHM: The pH scale measures the logarithmic concentration of hydrogen ions. Neutral pH is precisely 7.0. Any value below 7.0 is acidic, representing a high density of free protons. Any value above 7.0 is basic (alkaline).\n\n2. OXIDATION POTENTIALS: Oxidation represents a fundamental chemical reaction where a molecule or atom releases valence electrons to a catalytic medium. The substance that loses electrons is oxidized. The substance that gains them is reduced.\n\n3. ACID-BASE CONJUGATES: A conjugate base is the chemical species remaining after an acid has donated a proton. For instance, when bisulfate (HSO4-) donates its proton, it transforms into its conjugate base, sulfate (SO4^2-).\n\n4. LIQUID DISPENSING: A percent solution represents grams of solute dissolved in one hundred milliliters of solvent. A 10% solution therefore contains exactly 10 grams of alchemical salt per 100 mL of total liquid.","TOME II: PHARMACEUTICAL CHEMISTRY & ELECTROLYTE KINETICS"),A.ado("HUMAN ANATOMY & PHYSIOLOGY\n\n1. THE SKELETAL SYSTEM: The femur is the longest and strongest bone in the human skeletal framework, located inside the thigh. The humerus is the long bone of the upper arm, running from the shoulder joint to the elbow.\n\n2. PACEMAKER CURRENT: Cardiac pace and rhythm are coordinated by the sinoatrial (SA) node, which initiates spontaneous electrical depolarization waves across the atria.\n\n3. CRANIAL NERVES: The seventh cranial nerve (CN VII), commonly known as the facial nerve, controls all muscles of facial expression. Sensory trigeminal (CN V) manages facial sensation and mastication.\n\n4. SARCOMERE STRUCTURE: During active muscular contraction, the sarcomere shortens. The A band, representing thick myosin filaments, remains completely constant in length. Conversely, the I band and the H zone contract and shorten.","TOME III: DE HUMANI CORPORIS FABRICA: CLINICAL ANATOMY"),A.ado("SURGERY, DISPENSING & TRIAGE\n\n1. ABDOMINAL INCISIONS: From superficial to deep, a surgeon must incise through: Skin, Camper's fascia (superficial fatty layer), Scarpa's fascia (deep membranous layer), External oblique muscle, Internal oblique muscle, and Transversus abdominis.\n\n2. CARDIAC ISCHEMIA: A sudden-onset radiating chest pain accompanied by ST-segment elevations on a cardiograph indicates a severe ST-elevation myocardial infarction (STEMI), requiring immediate arterial reperfusion.\n\n3. REAGENT STORAGE: High-potency refined organic elixirs undergo photolytic degradation when exposed to ambient ultraviolet light. Storing them in amber glass vials absorbs light wavelengths and prevents degradation.\n\n4. DOSAGE CALCULATIONS: Pediatric and specialized dosages require multiplying the patient's weight in kilograms by the dosage per kilogram. If a patient weighs 80 kg and requires 5 mg/kg of a reagent, they require 400 mg total.","TOME IV: CLINICAL PATHOLOGY & SURGICAL METHODS")],A.aE("K<Sj>")))
s($,"c51","bPl",()=>{var q="None of the below",p=t.s
return A.a([A.au(A.a(["Flaubert","Giles","Kael","Alphonse"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 1:\nFour scholars (Flaubert, Giles, Alphonse, Kael) speak. Alphonse speaks third. Giles speaks immediately after Kael. Who speaks first?"),A.au(A.a(["A","B","C","D"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 2:\nA must perform before B. C must perform immediately after D. D is scheduled second. Who performs first?"),A.au(A.a(["No teachers are politicians","Some politicians are teachers","All teachers are politicians","None"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 3:\nNo politicians are honest. All teachers are honest. Therefore, which is true?"),A.au(A.a(["X is older than Z","Z is older than X","Y is younger than Z","None"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 4:\nIf X is older than Y, and Y is older than Z, which must be true?"),A.au(A.a(["Some novelists are academic","No novelists are academic","All academics are novelists","None"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 5:\nSome novelists are historians. All historians are academic. Therefore, which must be true?"),A.au(A.a(["B","A","C","Cannot tell"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 6:\nEvent A occurs before B. C occurs after B. If C is third, which is second?"),A.au(A.a([q,"Zombies are constructs","All constructs are slow","No constructs are slow"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 7:\nEvery zombie is slow. Some slow entities are constructs. Therefore, which is true?"),A.au(A.a(["Giles does not attend","Giles must attend","Flaubert attends","Kael does not attend"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 8:\nGiles attends only if Flaubert attends. Flaubert never attends if Kael is present. If Kael is present:"),A.au(A.a(["2","1","3","4"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 9:\nFive cases (1, 2, 3, 4, 5) are filed. 3 is filed after 2. 1 is before 2. 5 is last. Which is filed second?"),A.au(A.a(["Cannot be determined","Kael","Giles","Flaubert"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 10:\nIf Kael is older than Giles, and Giles is younger than Flaubert, who is the youngest?"),A.au(A.a(["Some Glarus workers are not alchemists","All Glarus workers are alchemists","No alchemists are Glarus workers","None"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 11:\nNo alchemists are members. Some members are Glarus workers. Therefore:"),A.au(A.a(["Contract A is not void","Contract A is void","Contract B is void","None"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 12:\nIf contract A is void, then contract B is also void. Contract B is not void. Therefore:"),A.au(A.a(["Some metallic entities are reanimated","All metallic entities are reanimated","No reanimated entities are metallic","None"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 13:\nAll constructs are metallic. Some constructs are reanimated. Therefore:"),A.au(A.a(["Giles retirement is undetermined","Giles must retire","Giles does not retire","Alphonse retires"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 14:\nIf Alphonse graduates, Giles retires. Alphonse does not graduate. Therefore:"),A.au(A.a(["Reagent 3","Reagent 2","Reagent 1","Reagent 4"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 15:\nFour elixirs are ranked. Reagent 1 is better than 2. Reagent 3 is worse than 2. Reagent 4 is equal to 1. Which is the worst?"),A.au(A.a(["Covenants require consideration","Covenants do not require consideration","Consideration requires covenants","None"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 16:\nEvery contract requires consideration. Covenants are contracts. Therefore:"),A.au(A.a(["Kael is not in Rolle","Kael is in Rolle","Kael is in Lausanne","None"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 17:\nIf Kael is in Rolle, Giles is in Rolle. Giles is in Lausanne. Therefore:"),A.au(A.a(["Some elixirs are not healthy drinks","All elixirs are healthy drinks","No healthy drinks are elixirs","None"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 18:\nSome elixirs are poisonous. No healthy drinks are poisonous. Therefore:"),A.au(A.a(["Construct 1 is slow","Construct 1 is fast","Construct 2 is slow","None"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 19:\nIf construct 1 is fast, construct 2 is slow. Construct 2 is fast. Therefore:"),A.au(A.a([q,"Some lawyers are corrupt","No lawyers are corrupt","All educated are lawyers"],p),0,"LSAT ANALYTICAL 20:\nAll lawyers are educated. Some educated are corrupt. Therefore:")],t.nz)})
s($,"c50","bPk",()=>{var q="Adverse possession",p="Beyond a reasonable doubt",o="Reasonable suspicion",n=t.s
return A.a([A.au(A.a(["Second cousin once removed","Third cousin","Second cousin","First cousin twice removed"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 1:\nIn legal kinship consanguinity, what is the precise term for your grandmother's cousin's granddaughter?"),A.au(A.a(["Offer, Acceptance, and Consideration","Agreement, Signature, and Notarization","Offer, Witnessing, and Collateral","Filing, Registration, and Fee Payment"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 2:\nWhat are the three core, globally foundational elements required to form a legally binding contract?"),A.au(A.a(["An out-of-court statement offered to prove the truth of the matter asserted.","Direct visual observation testified to by a witness.","A written contract signed by both parties.","An anatomy treatise description."],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 3:\nWhich of the following qualifies as 'hearsay' in common law jurisdictions?"),A.au(A.a(["Negligence","Trespass","Libel","Battery"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 4:\nWhat is the term for an unintentional civil wrong resulting from a failure to take reasonable care?"),A.au(A.a(["Mens rea","Actus reus","Habeas corpus","Stare decisis"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 5:\nWhat is the term for the mental intent required to constitute a crime in international legal theory?"),A.au(A.a(["Intestate succession","Probate covenant","Escheatment",q],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 6:\nWhat is the term for the transfer of property ownership to another upon death without a valid will?"),A.au(A.a(["Specific performance","Injunction","Damages","Rescission"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 7:\nWhat is the legal term for a court order forcing a party to perform a specific act required by contract?"),A.au(A.a(["Contracts for the sale of land interests","Contracts for minor household services","Agreements to water garden beds","Contracts under 50 CHF value"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 8:\nUnder the statute of frauds, which of the following contracts must always be in writing to be enforceable?"),A.au(A.a(["Duress","Undue influence","Misrepresentation","Mistake"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 9:\nWhat is the legal term for a contract where one party is unfairly coerced or threatened into signing?"),A.au(A.a(["Necessity","Duress","Self-defense","Entrapment"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 10:\nWhich defense completely excuses criminal liability if the defendant acted to prevent an imminent greater harm?"),A.au(A.a([p,"Preponderance of evidence","Clear and convincing evidence",o],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 11:\nWhat is the standard of proof required to convict a defendant in a criminal trial?"),A.au(A.a(["Escheat",q,"Emminent domain","Intestacy"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 12:\nWhat is the term for property that reverts to the state because there are no legal heirs or wills?"),A.au(A.a(["Punitive damages","Compensatory damages","Nominal damages","Liquidated damages"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 13:\nWhich type of damage aims to punish a defendant for extremely reckless or malicious behavior?"),A.au(A.a(["Libel","Slander","Negligence","Assault"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 14:\nWhat is the term for a written defamation that harms a person's reputation?"),A.au(A.a(["Accord and satisfaction","Novation","Rescission","Breach of contract"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 15:\nWhat is the legal term for an agreement to accept a different performance than what was originally contracted?"),A.au(A.a(["Stare decisis","Res judicata","Obiter dictum","Ratio decidendi"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 16:\nWhich legal doctrine stands for the principle that past judicial decisions bind future decisions?"),A.au(A.a(["Immaterial breach","Material breach","Anticipatory repudiation","Fundamental breach"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 17:\nWhat is the term for a minor contract breach that does not excuse the non-breaching party from performance?"),A.au(A.a(["Oral contract","Implied contract","Formal contract","Adhesion contract"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 18:\nWhich type of contract is formed by spoken words rather than written text?"),A.au(A.a(["Option contract","Firm offer","Counteroffer","Gratuitous promise"],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 19:\nWhat is the term for an offer that remains open for a specified time because consideration was paid?"),A.au(A.a(["Preponderance of the evidence",p,"Clear and convincing",o],n),0,"LAW ACADEMIC 20:\nWhich standard of proof is utilized in standard civil tort trials?")],t.nz)})
